; Example: UEB emergency-stop input (Universal Electronics Box / Scylla).
; Copy to 0:/sys/estop.g and pair with trigger2.g (from trigger2.g.example).
; Board pack loads estop.g before gpio.g; nxt.g runs nxt-relay.g when both exist.
;
; SAFETY-CRITICAL. The E-stop has two NC contacts:
;   - Contact 1 is in series with the 24V to the contactor (with the relay,
;     PD_5 / alias relay, also relayctr) and cuts motor/VFD power in HARDWARE,
;     independent of firmware.
;   - Contact 2 is wired to PC6 here, so the FIRMWARE can detect the E-stop
;     and react: drop gpOut P5 (M42) and emergency-stop (see trigger2.g).
; Board pack gpio.g creates the latch as gpOut P5 on PD_5 (not RRF ATX).
;
; >>> VERIFY INPUT LOGIC ON HARDWARE <<<
; Built assuming the input reads ACTIVE (value 1) when the E-stop is PRESSED
; (contact 2 open). After deploying, check in the console:
;     echo sensors.gpIn[0].value
;   E-stop released -> should read 0 ;  pressed -> should read 1.
; If it's reversed, invert the pin: change C"^PC6" to C"^!PC6" below (that
; flips both the reading AND the trigger edge together). The "^" enables the
; internal pull-up - remove it only if the input has a hardware pull-up.

M950 J0 C"^PC6"          ; E-stop input (2nd NC contact), pull-up enabled
M581 P0 T2 S1 R0         ; on E-stop PRESSED (inactive->active), run trigger2.g, always
